<article class="env-proposition" id="06ET">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06ET">Proposition <span data-tag="06ET">9.2.7.13</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \aleph _0}$ be the $\infty $-category of finitely dominated $\infty $-categories. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \aleph _0 }$ is essentially $\aleph _1$-small: that is, it is equivalent to an $\infty $-category having finitely many simplices. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By virtue of Proposition <a data-tag="0410" href="/tag/0410">8.5.5.7</a>, it will suffice to show that the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{ \mathrm{fin} }$ is essentially $\aleph _1$-small. Since the collection of isomorphism classes of finite simplicial sets is countable (Variant <a data-tag="05YP" href="/tag/05YP">4.9.4.21</a>), the collection of isomorphism classes of objects of $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{ \mathrm{fin} }$ is also countable. It will therefore suffice to show that the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{ \mathrm{fin} }$ is locally $\aleph _1$-small. Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be essentially finite $\infty $-categories; we wish to show that the morphism space $\operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}} ( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \simeq \operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})^{\simeq }$ is essentially $\aleph _1$-small (see Remark <a data-tag="020F" href="/tag/020F">5.5.3.5</a>). Without loss of generality, we may assume that $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is $\aleph _1$-small. Since $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is essentially finite, there is a categorical equivalence $e: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, where $K$ is a finite simplicial set. Then composition with $e$ induces a homotopy equivalence from $\operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})^{\simeq }$ to the Kan complex $\operatorname{Fun}( K, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})^{\simeq }$, which is $\aleph _1$-small by virtue of Corollary <a data-tag="03SG" href="/tag/03SG">4.9.4.19</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
